      "claim": "Levosulpiride, a methoxy-substituted benzamide with a basic amine side chain, has an oral bioavailability of about 30% in healthy volunteers.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C71"],
      "claim": "One verapamil study reported a mean bioavailability of 19.4%, slightly below the 20% threshold, indicating borderline first-pass liability in the closest analogue.",
